&lt;h3 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;Shift: Full time 40 hour a week role, Monday-Friday 9am-5pm with some weekend flexibility.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;About Avride&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Avride is a U.S.-based autonomous vehicle startup headquartered in Austin, TX, with additional R&amp;amp;D hubs around the world. Our company develops and operates both autonomous cars and delivery robots that share technologies and mutually benefit from each other’s advancements—a unique approach in the industry. Since 2017, Avride has been building expertise in autonomous technologies to create solutions that address current needs and anticipate future demands. Today, we operate a fleet of autonomous vehicles in Dallas, Texas, in partnership with Uber, bringing our technology into real-world deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Avride is preparing to launch a fleet of autonomous delivery robots at Fairfield University and is seeking a hands-on Robot Service Technician to support this exciting deployment. In this role, you will be responsible for the assembly, maintenance, troubleshooting, repair, and field operation of our autonomous delivery robots. This position is ideal for someone who enjoys solving complex technical problems, working across mechanical and electrical systems, and contributing to the advancement of cutting-edge robotics technology in a fast-paced, real-world environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;Shift&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, 40-hour-per-week position. Standard hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM, with some flexibility required for earlier start times or later end times based on business needs. The 40-hour weekly schedule may also include weekend hours (Saturday and/or Sunday) as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production &amp;amp; assembly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assemble wiring harnesses, cables, and connectors for autonomous delivery robots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, configure, and replace sensors including LiDAR, cameras, and ultrasonic sensors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform mechanical and electrical assembly of robot components and subsystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow technical documentation, schematics, and assembly procedures to ensure quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintenance &amp;amp; repair&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform routine maintenance and preventive service on the robot fleet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose failures, investigate incidents, and execute repair and service campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test, troubleshoot, and repair mechanical and electrical systems, including suspension and battery components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document maintenance activities and service findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field operations support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel between local sites to provide onsite technical support as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support deployment, testing, and validation of autonomous delivery robots in real-world environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with inventory management, equipment tracking, and parts organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in rapid prototyping and hardware validation efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Need&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using mechanical and electrical tools, including measuring equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience assembling and disassembling electrical and electromechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret 2D mechanical drawings and technical documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience installing and integrating custom electronic modules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of AC/DC electrical systems and safe working practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license with a clean driving record&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working both in a workshop environment and in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and move items weighing 50 pounds or more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and a methodical approach to troubleshooting and problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent teamwork, communication, and collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable, proactive mindset with the ability to handle a variety of technical tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in automotive service, vehicle retrofitting, manufacturing, or related industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with electric vehicles (EVs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soldering and wire crimping experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General computer proficiency and familiarity with diagnostic tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting robotics, autonomous systems, or other advanced technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer Subsidized Healthcare Benefits thru our 3rd party employer of record partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Account for healthcare-related costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short and long-term disability and life insurance thru our 3rd party employer of record partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a full-time, ongoing contract position staffed through our trusted Employer of Record partner, who manages payroll, benefits, and local compliance on our behalf. You will work day-to-day with the Avride team and be fully integrated into our culture and operations. This job is onsite and available to candidates local to the Miami, FL area.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em class=&quot;italic-text&quot;&gt;Candidates are required to be authorized to work in the U.S. The employer is not offering relocation, sponsorship, and remote work options are not available.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
