&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is responsible for building the internal systems for the whole engineering team. Our goal is to help engineers navigate across all produced data, investigate problems, and create ad hoc analytics. Our services are used daily across the company: by QA engineers verifying component-level quality, by autonomy engineers investigating unexpected behavior, by ML teams validating new model versions, by safety analysts and data scientists who analyze thousands of scenarios and metrics to assess system readiness, and by release engineers who test our products on public roads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Frontend Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to help us push the boundaries of what web interfaces can do. You’ll be responsible for developing several projects. For example, we have the Simulator as a service. This service helps engineers to reproduce scenarios from real-world rides and calculate metrics. You will build tools to help with mining scenarios, organize them, track simulations, and collect metrics. Another example is the fleet-tracking service. It handles our cars’ and robots’ locations, their building progress, installed equipment, and configuring autopilot to work properly according to the setup. You will develop a system that allows us to safely update the hardware and software setup of our production fleet.&lt;/p&gt;
