&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;About Avride&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Avride is a U.S.-based autonomous vehicle startup headquartered in Austin, TX, with additional R&amp;amp;D hubs around the world. Our company develops and operates both autonomous cars and delivery robots that share technologies and mutually benefit from each other’s advancements—a unique approach in the industry. Since 2017, Avride has been building expertise in autonomous technologies to create solutions that address current needs and anticipate future demands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a reliable Support Specialists to support the day-to-day technical operations of an autonomous vehicle fleet in Austin.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is primarily a technical support role focused on real-time issue intake, triage, documentation, and escalation. The person in this role will work closely with safety drivers, operators, and engineering teams to keep vehicles operational and ensure technical issues are clearly captured and routed for further debugging.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate has a general technical support background, is comfortable working in Unix command line environments on a daily basis, communicates clearly, and can stay organized while handling multiple requests in a fast-paced operational setting. This role also includes light hands-on vehicle support, such as basic readiness checks, cable reconnections, and occasional vehicle movement within the garage.&lt;/p&gt;
