&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the first point of contact for technical issues raised by safety drivers and operators during active shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process, triage, document, and escalate vehicle- and system-related issues to the appropriate engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Unix command line tools regularly to support issue investigation, log review, and operational troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with operators, drivers, and engineers to ensure issues are accurately understood and handed off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support vehicle dispatch and return processes to help maintain fleet readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform vehicle startup and shutdown procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee charging status and confirm log uploads as part of daily operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform light hands-on support tasks such as reconnecting cables, checking onboard device indicators, and confirming system readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move vehicles around the garage as needed and be prepared to drive on-road occasionally if required in the future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help document updates to workflows, procedures, and support practices so knowledge can be shared across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
